I stand at the machine in the station.
Today I must travel with the U-Bahn and then change trains.
I need a ticket for the whole journey.
I tap quickly on the screen.
The ticket costs three Euro fifty.
I want to pay, but nothing happens.
Then I see the problem.
On the screen it says: "Out of order".
This machine is broken.
A woman stands next to me.
"Excuse me, this machine does not work," she says.
"But at the end of the platform is another machine."
She points to the end of the platform.
"You can buy your ticket there."
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
I run quickly to the other machine.
Here everything works very well.
I choose the ticket and pay three Euro fifty.
The ticket comes out of the machine.
Now I have my ticket for the journey.
